course: dictionary
lesson: 7400
title: Words from the modern world
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are new because they name things that did not exist when your grandparents were young. «Grandma asked for "Dancing Queen" and got a podcast about queens.» Grandma wanted a song, but the sentence says she got a show instead, so a podcast must be something different from a song.
explain: Look at the words around the new word. «Listen to a podcast» tells you a podcast is something you can listen to. «A new episode of the podcast» tells you a podcast has many episodes, like a TV series. Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence and asking if it still makes sense.
explain: Podcast can also be a verb. «She wants to start a podcast about space» shows that a podcast can be made as well as heard. Some words change their job in a sentence, so the clues tell you which job the word is doing.
fact: A podcast is a series of audio shows on the internet, and sometimes they include video.
fact: You can download or stream a podcast and listen whenever you like.
fact: One episode of a podcast is also called a podcast.
fact: To podcast means to make and publish these shows.
fact: Podcasts can share opinions, so it is wise to check facts from more than one source.
exercise: What is a podcast? | *A series of audio shows on the internet that you can listen to whenever you like | A kind of dance from the 1970s | A printed magazine sent through the post | A map of the internet
exercise: «Grandma asked for "Dancing Queen" and got a podcast about queens.» What did Grandma want, and what did she get instead? | She wanted a map and got a book | She wanted a podcast and got a song | *She wanted a song and got a podcast | She wanted a film and got a painting
exercise: «She wants to start a podcast about space.» What does start a podcast mean here? | To fall asleep while reading | To delete an old book | To buy a new phone | *To make and publish a new show
test: «I listened to a new episode of the podcast on dinosaurs.» What is one episode of a podcast? | A book about dinosaurs | The whole phone it was played on | A picture of a dinosaur | *One show from the series
test: In the sentence «She will podcast every Friday», what does podcast mean? | To bake a cake | To draw a map | *To make and publish a show | To swim in a pool
exam: Why should you check facts from a podcast before you believe them? | Because podcasts are always wrong | Because podcasts cannot be heard on phones | Because podcasts are only for music | *Because podcasts can share opinions, not just facts
